# Files Lash should ignore when indexing this repo.
#
# We dogfood Lash via `lash.index.md` at the repo root for current/near-term
# work. Everything below either predates Lash's task-file format or is
# documentation, fixtures, or output that has its own structure.

# Documentation
README.md
CLAUDE.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
DEVELOPMENT_PLAN.md
devlog.md
test-coverage-analysis.md
docs/
demos/

# Sample/fixture projects used by tests and walkthroughs — these *are* in
# lash task-file format but they're examples, not real work.
examples/

# Historical task breakdown predating Lash's own linter; kept for archival
# reference and PR descriptions, not indexed by Lash itself.
tasks/

# Rust source — any `.md` in here is test fixtures (incl. intentionally
# broken ones), benchmarks, or doctest data, not real task tracking.
crates/

# Other build/asset directories.
assets/

